  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Your 401(k) balance isn't just a number. Each level buys a very different retirement. Let's climb them.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Each balance,",
            "a different retirement."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Using the four percent rule, each hundred thousand saved pays about four thousand a year, for life.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "Balance → yearly income",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "$100K",
              "value": "$4K/yr",
              "note": "a supplement",
              "color": "#5c544c",
              "bar": 0.1
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "$500K",
              "value": "$20K/yr",
              "note": "with Social Security, okay",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.4
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "$1M",
              "value": "$40K/yr",
              "note": "comfortable",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.7
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "$2.5M",
              "value": "$100K/yr",
              "note": "the dream",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Your retirement income is really driven by your final balance.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-retirement",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · retirement"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So to retire on a given income, you need roughly twenty-five times your annual spending saved.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "× 25",
          "label": "spending = your target",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Most people build it inside a tax-advantaged 401(k).",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-401k",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · 401(k)"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And incredibly, over five hundred thousand ordinary people have reached a million, just by being consistent.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "500K+",
          "label": "ordinary 401(k) millionaires",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "They did it with compounding and time, not huge salaries.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-compound",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · compound interest"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The real target isn't a round million, it's twenty-five times whatever you actually spend.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "25× spending",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Your final balance is entirely down to what you contribute.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-dc",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · defined contribution"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Consistency, not a giant salary, is what quietly built most of them.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Consistency wins",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So which balance level, and which retirement, is actually yours?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "bank",
          "line": "Which is yours?",
          "sub": "Comment your level"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s11"
    }
  ]
